+// Linux stand-in for Darwin's hole punching (hle_svc.c guest_file_punch): the host gives
+// back the disk blocks a released range held. macOS does it with
+// fcntl(F_PUNCHHOLE, {offset, length}); Linux has the same operation with the same numbers
+// under a different name, F_PUNCH_HOLE (4 on every arch this builds for), and a struct the
+// kernel reads the same way. Where the kernel has no hole punching the call answers an
+// error, and the caller reports that as it does any failed punch.
+#ifndef F_PUNCH_HOLE
